  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The molar mass of an ideal gas is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span>. A fixed mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> of the gas expands at a constant pressure <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"p\"></span>. The graph shows the variation with temperature T of the gas volume V.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the gradient of the graph?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Mp}{mR}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{MR}{mp}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{mp}{MR}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{mR}{Mp}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
